@{
    ViewBag.Title = "CSS/LESS Rules";
}
<div class="col-sm-12">
    <ul class="rule-list">
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC001">OWC001 Must use LESS for your styling code</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC002">OWC002 Use valid CSS where possible</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC003">OWC003 Remove all trailing whitespaces</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC004">OWC004 Use spaces instead of tabs</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC005">OWC005 Use meaningful or generic ID and class names</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC006">OWC006 Use ID and class names that are as short as possible but as long as necessary</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC007">OWC007 Avoid qualifying ID and class name with type selectors</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC008">OWC008 Prefer using class names as selectors to IDs</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC009">OWC009 Avoid descendant selector as possible</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC010">OWC010 Use shorthand properties where possible</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC011">OWC011 Omit unit specification after “0” values</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC012">OWC012 Omit leading “0”s in values between -1 and 1</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC013">OWC013 For color values, use 3 character hexadecimal notation where possible</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC014">OWC014 Separate words in ID and class names by a hyphen</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC015">OWC015 Put declarations in alphabetical order</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC016">OWC016 Indent all blocks</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC017">OWC017 Use a semicolon after every declaration</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC018">OWC018 Always use a single space between property and value (but no space between property and colon)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC019">OWC019 Use a space between the last selector and the declaration block</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC020">OWC020 Always put a blank line between rules</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC021">OWC021 Use single quotation marks for attribute selectors and property values. Exception: If you do need to use the <code>@@charset</code> rule, use double quotation marks</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="link-sub-title" code="OWC022">OWC022 If possible, group stylesheet sections together by using comments. Separate sections with new lines.</a></li>
    </ul>
    <ul class="rules unordered">
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title first" id="OWC001"><span class="rule-item">OWC001 </span> Must use <a href="http://lesscss.org/" target="_blank">LESS</a> for your styling code</h2>
            <p>It adds features which allow variables, mixins, functions and many other techniques that make CSS be more maintainable, themeable and extendible.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC002"><span class="rule-item">OWC002 </span> Use valid CSS where possible</h2>
            <p>
                Unless dealing with CSS validator bugs or requiring proprietary syntax, you must ensure that your styling code is valid.
                Use tools such as the <a href="http://jigsaw.w3.org/css-validator/" target="_blank">W3C CSS validator</a> to test.
            </p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC003"><span class="rule-item">OWC003 </span> Remove all trailing whitespaces</h2>
            <p>
                The number of whitespaces for a tab may vary with many editors, thus using whitespace instead of tab helps to keep the format of code be the same.
                Do not use tabs or mix tabs and spaces for indentation.
            </p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC004"><span class="rule-item">OWC004 </span> Use spaces instead of tabs</h2>
            <p>The trailing whitespaces are unnecessary and can complicate diffs.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC005"><span class="rule-item">OWC005 </span> Use meaningful or generic ID and class names</h2>
            <p>
                Names that are specific and reflect the purpose of the element should be preferred since these are most understandable and the least likely to change.
                Using functional or generic names reduces the probability of unnecessary document or template changes.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended: meaningless */
                    #abc-123 {}
                </pre>
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended: specific */
                    #gallery {}
                    #login {}
                    .video {}
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC006"><span class="rule-item">OWC006 </span> Use ID and class names that are as short as possible but as long as necessary</h2>
            <p>
                Try to convey what an ID or class is about while being as brief as possible.
                It contributes to acceptable levels of understandability and code efficiency.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended */
                    #navigation {}
                    .atr {}
                </pre>
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    #nav {}
                    .author {}
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC007"><span class="rule-item">OWC007 </span> Avoid qualifying ID and class name with type selectors</h2>
            <p>
                It dues to performance reason.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended */
                    ul#example {}
                    div.error {}
                </pre>
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    #example {}
                    .error {}
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC008"><span class="rule-item">OWC008 </span> Prefer using class names as selectors to IDs</h2>
            <p>Using class name helps the CSS code is more independent from the JavaScript code.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC009"><span class="rule-item">OWC009 </span> Avoid descendant selector as possible</h2>
            <p>
                The descendant selectors are the most expensive selector in CSS.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended */
                    html body ul li a {
                        color: #fff;
                    }
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC010"><span class="rule-item">OWC010 </span> Use shorthand properties where possible</h2>
            <p>
                The shorthand properties are useful for code efficiency and understandability.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended */
                    border-top-style: none;
                    font-family: palatino, georgia, serif;
                    font-size: 100%;
                    line-height: 1.6;
                    padding-bottom: 2em;
                    padding-left: 1em;
                    padding-right: 1em;
                    padding-top: 0;
                </pre>
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    border-top: 0;
                    font: 100%/1.6 palatino, georgia, serif;
                    padding: 0 1em 2em;
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC011"><span class="rule-item">OWC011 </span> Omit unit specification after “0” values</h2>
            <div class="example-code none-top-content">
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    margin: 0;
                    padding: 0;
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC012"><span class="rule-item">OWC012 </span>Omit leading “0”s in values between -1 and 1</h2>
            <div class="example-code none-top-content">
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    font-size: .8em;
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC013"><span class="rule-item">OWC013 </span> For color values, use 3 character hexadecimal notation where possible</h2>
            <p>
                It make the code be shorter and more succinct.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended */
                    color: #eebbcc;
                </pre>
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    color: #ebc;
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC014"><span class="rule-item">OWC014 </span> Separate words in ID and class names by a hyphen</h2>
            <p>
                Do not concatenate words and abbreviations in selectors by any characters (including none at all) other than hyphens,
                in order to improve understanding and scannability.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended: does not separate the words “demo” and “image” */
                    .demoimage {}
                    /* Not recommended: uses underscore instead of hyphen */
                    .error_status {}
                </pre>
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    #video-id {}
                    .ads-sample {}
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC015"><span class="rule-item">OWC015 </span> Put declarations in alphabetical order</h2>
            <p>
                The purpose of this action is to achieve consistent code in a way that is easy to remember and maintain.
                Ignore vendor-specific prefixes for sorting purposes.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    border: 1px solid;
                    -moz-border-radius: 4px;
                    -webkit-border-radius: 4px;
                    border-radius: 4px;
                    color: black;
                    text-align: center;
                    text-indent: 2em;
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC016"><span class="rule-item">OWC016 </span> Indent all blocks</h2>
            <p>
                To reflect hierarchy and improve understanding.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    body {
                        border: 1px solid;
                        -moz-border-radius: 4px;
                        -webkit-border-radius: 4px;
                        .header {
                            text-align: center;
                            text-indent: 2em;
                        }
                    }
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC017"><span class="rule-item">OWC017 </span> Use a semicolon after every declaration</h2>
            <p>
                End every declaration with a semicolon for consistency and extensibility reasons.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended: the second declaration must end with a semicolon */
                    .test {
                      display: block;
                      height: 100px
                    }
                </pre>
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    .test {
                      display: block;
                      height: 100px;
                    }
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC018"><span class="rule-item">OWC018 </span> Always use a single space between property and value (but no space between property and colon)</h2>
            <div class="example-code none-top-content">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended */
                    h3 {
                      font-weight:bold;
                    }
                </pre>
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    h3 {
                      font-weight: bold;
                    }
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC019"><span class="rule-item">OWC019 </span> Use a space between the last selector and the declaration block</h2>
            <p>
                Always use a single space between the last selector and the opening brace that begins the declaration block.
                The opening brace should be on the same line as the last selector in a given rule.
            </p>
            <div class="example-code">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended: missing space */
                    #video{
                      margin-top: 1em;
                    }
                    /* Not recommended: unnecessary line break */
                    #video
                    {
                      margin-top: 1em;
                    }
                </pre>
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    #video {
                      margin-top: 1em;
                    }
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC020"><span class="rule-item">OWC020 </span> Always put a blank line between rules</h2>
            <div class="example-code none-top-content">
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    html {
                      background: #fff;
                    }
                    body {
                      margin: auto;
                      width: 50%;
                    }
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC021"><span class="rule-item">OWC021 </span> Use single quotation marks for attribute selectors and property values. Exception: If you do need to use the <code>@@charset</code> rule, use double quotation marks</h2>
            <div class="example-code none-top-content">
                <pre class="text-danger">
                    /* Not recommended */
                    @@import url("//www.google.com/css/maia.css");
                    html {
                      font-family: "open sans", arial, sans-serif;
                    }
                </pre>
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /* Recommended */
                    @@import url(//www.google.com/css/maia.css);
                    html {
                      font-family: 'open sans', arial, sans-serif;
                    }
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <h2 class="sub-title" id="OWC022"><span class="rule-item">OWC022 </span> If possible, group stylesheet sections together by using comments. Separate sections with new lines.</h2>
            <div class="example-code none-top-content">
                <pre class="text-success">
                    /********************************************************/
                    /*                        Header                        */
                    /********************************************************/
                    .header {
                        background-color: @@primary-color;
                        height: 50px;
                        .logo {
                            background: url(Images/logo.png) no-repeat;
                            width: 210px;
                            height: 16px;
                            display: inline-block;
                        }
                    }
                    /********************************************************/
                    /*                        Content                       */
                    /********************************************************/
                    .content {
                        position: absolute;
                        top: 50px;
                    }
                </pre>
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>
@section scripts
{
    @Scripts.Render("~/bundles/rules/js")
}